  "claims": [
    "Two new explicit unit overlap pairs have common endpoints: expanding the final left/right unit then beta takes two forward steps; associating then expanding copy and beta takes three forward steps. Atomic scalar equality is exactly c13=c0+c9 and c14=c0+c9 respectively.",
    "Four bounded local diagram forms extend and retain the pure Fin 27 basis: fst/snd tensor-expansion projection overlaps with seven-versus-one equational rewrite leaves, plus left/right unit-expansion copy/projection overlaps with two-versus-three forward leaves. The new pure tag catalogue is Fin 31 and all boundaries have at most seven leaves, including contextual placement.",
    "The new tensor/projected boundaries each use one inverse association. No forward confluence or termination result is inferred.",
    "The previous pure higher cells embed in the new basis. Generic atomic output observation reconstruction is instantiated without adding whole-normalization or arbitrary semantic equality generators.",
    "Given an atom, preservation of the restricted constant-output eighteen-root integer annotation class by the new Fin 31 basis is equivalent to exactly the previous five constraints plus c8+c9+c3+c1=0, c13=c9 and c14=c9. Both necessity and sufficiency for all typed generators are proved.",
    "A tensor/projection atomic comparison now exists in the new pure basis while the previous pure basis cannot derive it. A right-unit/copy projection comparison was also absent before the extension. No minimality or independence of all four added forms is asserted.",
    "Routed annotations are additive in the coefficient function. Every actual path weight is a sum of the eighteen unit-coordinate path weights with the corresponding integer coefficients.",
    "For the selected first atomic projection of the actual canonical tensor example, the difference of weights is exactly -4*c0+2*c1+4*c3-2*c5+2*c7+2*c8+c9+c14. All eighteen unit-coordinate differences are proved by kernel reduction, and the general formula uses the additive decomposition.",
    "Every annotation in this restricted class preserving the new Fin 31 basis gives equal weights on that selected atomic comparison. This removes that class of obstruction there; it does not construct a higher comparison or prove canonical tensor coherence.",
    "The mixed extension retains the previous mixed distribution library, embeds new pure cells with empty support, and preserves the actual retained MAC sum and its embedding constructor counts.",
    "The previous three-family MAC/erasure/sequential-fusion contract is retargeted unchanged, including the original stage and stage+1 framed support.",
    "An actual new tensor/projection local comparison is placed after a shared MAC.before stage computation. Its support is exactly singleton stage. Repaired joint-law equality in the updated checked model retains the correlated past, input and state."
  ],
  "finite_scope": {
    "pure_schematic_tag_count": 31,
    "new_schematic_families": 4,
    "max_boundary_rewrite_leaves": 7,
    "unit_new_boundaries": [
      2,
      3
    ],
    "tensor_projection_new_boundaries": [
      7,
      1
    ],
    "annotation_domain": "18 integer coefficients constant on each output atom per root, routed through actual wires",
    "exact_constraints": [
      "c0=0",
      "c1=c2",
      "c5=c3",
      "c5=c4",
      "c7=0",
      "c8+c9+c3+c1=0",
      "c13=c9",
      "c14=c9"
    ],
    "necessity_assumption": "one supplied element of Atom",
    "profile_scope": "The selected first atomic output projection of the frozen actual tensor normalization example, not every atom, every wire, every invariant or a constructed higher proof",
    "mixed_contract_catalogue": "The previous three source families only"
  },
  "limits": [
    "Fin 31 counts typed schematic forms, not a finite set of concrete instances or a complete higher basis for the full eighteen-root/mixed catalogue.",
    "Only the four explicit local comparisons are added. There is no exhaustive classifier for arbitrary coinitial steps.",
    "All scalar classification and discrepancy claims are limited to constant-output integer root annotations. Their equality is a necessary condition for a higher comparison, not a sufficient condition. No universal natural system or complete decision method is proved.",
    "The actual canonical tensor normalization square remains without a constructed higher witness. The generic tensor reconstruction still requires actual atomic higher witnesses.",
    "Seven-versus-one and two-versus-three count rewrite leaves. They omit groupoid constructors, wire/context payloads and checker time. No fair total-cost compression advantage is shown.",
    "The sampled local structural comparison has singleton stage because the prefix is MAC.before. It is not the MAC before/after crypto rewrite with stage and stage+1 conditions.",
    "No new code-changing reduction, advantage/loss/time bound or full continuing physical execution through oracle internals/keygen is supplied. Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC integration remains excluded.",
    "Mathematical novelty remains unconfirmed. Additive coefficient decomposition and local coherence methods are not claimed as new abstract principles. No new external primary-source reading or independent review occurred in this stage."
  ],
  "next_obligations": [
    "Construct actual syntactic atomic higher comparisons in the new basis for the canonical tensor square; do not substitute vanishing scalar annotations for those witnesses.",
    "Investigate any further missing bounded local diagrams and prove finite schematic coverage of all actual eighteen roots and mixed rules.",
    "Keep the full research goal active: code-changing reductions/losses/resources, continuing oracle/keygen execution, fair shared-proof total costs and primary-source theorem-level novelty assessment."
  ],
